WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Explosions sounded in Riyadh while the kingdom readied its principal airport for reopening after

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:10.900
Houthi strikes. This is Omni View, episode 216. Pakistan's reopen frontier with Iran,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.520
Serbia's Snap Parliamentary Vote, and a Prague exhibition on Roma wartime fighters follow,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:23.040
then understanding the issue. Saudi Arabia heads a coalition at war with the Iran-backed Houthis in Yemen.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.820
The kingdom has taken repeated strikes in recent weeks. The Hindu reported that the Indian mission

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.100
told its nationals not to film missile interceptions that Air India and Air India Express

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.140
had halted flights to and from Riyadh and Damam and cast the day as part of continuing

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.720
Houthi strikes across the region. Those flight cuts have affected routes from India.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.160
United States' help in Deutsche Bell is telling runs through an artificial intelligence or AI

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:55.660
targeting tool similar to the Maven smart system. Between 100 and 200 American personnel are on

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.480
the ground inside a newly formed joint force command.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.960
The partnership includes real-time visualization of battlefield data from satellite feeds and

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:04.740
drone cameras.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.760
Experts in that same reporting flag technological, political, and human rights issues with such

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.240
systems.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.460
The Maven Smart System gathers intelligence data.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.960
It labels potential targets such as rocket launchers or vehicle convoys.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.580
It also calculates optimal strike methods.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:27.494
operations resumed at the gabbed rimdan crossing with Iran after a week-long halt that

00:01:27.494 --> 00:01:28.634
had disrupted trade.

00:01:29.074 --> 00:01:33.334
The Hindu international treated the reopening as a practical step to address domestic

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.514
supply problems that followed the suspension.

00:01:36.314 --> 00:01:41.234
Officials expect the restart to ease shortages of liquefied petroleum gas or LPG.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.734
They also expect less pressure on food and energy prices.

00:01:45.374 --> 00:01:49.274
The aim is lower costs for households that paid more while the crossing was shut.

00:01:49.274 --> 00:01:53.814
That reporting tied the closure directly to price pressures inside Pakistan.

00:01:54.394 --> 00:01:58.754
The crossing is a key route for goods that shape everyday energy and food availability.

00:01:59.831 --> 00:02:04.891
A student-led list went to voters across Serbia, seeking to end the long rule of Alexander

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.091
Vuchich's party.

00:02:06.691 --> 00:02:10.731
Poles opened in a snap parliamentary vote after nearly two years of protests.

00:02:11.371 --> 00:02:16.551
Those demonstrations were triggered by a 2024 railway station canopy collapse that killed

00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:17.471
16 people.

00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:22.771
a failure widely attributed to corruption. The South China Morning Post described the

00:02:22.771 --> 00:02:27.911
contest as the most hard fought in more than 14 years and stressed the student movement's

00:02:27.911 --> 00:02:31.451
anti-corruption focus and the scale of protests since that disaster.

00:02:32.311 --> 00:02:37.471
Deutschewelle casts the same ballot as a possible break from Vuchich's hold, with students trying

00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:41.971
to remove the veteran leader through the vote rather than the street. The strongest case

00:02:41.971 --> 00:02:46.731
Vuchich's party makes is that continuity has delivered the stability and economic growth

00:02:46.731 --> 00:02:51.571
Serbian needs after years of turbulence, and that infrastructure finished under its watch

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:54.431
shows experienced government producing visible results.

00:02:54.971 --> 00:03:00.091
The student-led movement argues that persistent corruption has worn down public trust, and

00:03:00.091 --> 00:03:04.231
that new accountability is required to stop another tragedy like the canopy collapse.

00:03:04.971 --> 00:03:08.971
The oversight failures exposed by that collapse are not in dispute between them.

00:03:09.511 --> 00:03:14.111
They split on whether the present leadership can credibly repair those failures, or whether

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.391
new actors have to do it.

00:03:15.391 --> 00:03:20.674
The museum of the Romani National Revival in Prague opened a new exhibition on more

00:03:20.674 --> 00:03:25.774
than 1,400 Roma who fought as partisans and soldiers against Nazi occupation.

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:27.434
Deutscheweller reported.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:32.334
The display presents detailed accounts of 100 fighters chosen from the archives.

00:03:32.874 --> 00:03:38.954
It marks October 15, 2026, as a milestone for more than half a million Roma in Czechia

00:03:38.954 --> 00:03:39.854
and Slovakia.

00:03:40.474 --> 00:03:45.174
Czech and Slovak Roma have historically been portrayed almost exclusively as victims of

00:03:45.174 --> 00:03:50.534
the Holocaust. Roughly 90% of Czech Roma were killed in the protectorate of Bohemia and

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:56.554
Moravia during World War II. Museum director Emil Skuka said the exhibition aims to show Roma

00:03:56.554 --> 00:04:01.914
as both victims and heroes, and to address a topic long marginalized in historical writing.

00:04:02.454 --> 00:04:06.514
He called on attendees to bring children and grandchildren to see the stories of these

00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:12.954
fighters. Exhibition curator Radoslav Skuka said the team found more than 1,400 Romani

00:04:12.954 --> 00:04:17.774
fighters in the archives and selected the 100 most interesting stories for display.

00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:27.103
Research examining more than 1,700 administrations from 2019 found that 44% of prepag deals involving

00:04:27.103 --> 00:04:31.283
connected parties resulted in a second insolvency by July 2026.

00:04:32.003 --> 00:04:35.063
The rate was 26% when the buyer was unconnected.

00:04:35.463 --> 00:04:40.703
The Guardian commissioned the study from Turnstone Intelligence, which used AI agents to review

00:04:40.703 --> 00:04:41.683
official documents.

00:04:41.683 --> 00:04:41.843
investments.

00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:45.243
Connected party deals more often allowed deferred payments.

00:04:45.843 --> 00:04:50.643
Sixty-five percent of those cases permitted former owners and directors to re-acquire assets

00:04:50.643 --> 00:04:55.083
through future installments, compared with 28% for unconnected buyers.

00:04:55.743 --> 00:05:00.303
Former owners and directors frequently take assets back through installment plans, with

00:05:00.303 --> 00:05:05.583
consequences for unsecured creditors including HM Revenue and Customs, which estimates that

00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:09.083
Phoenix's M cost taxpayers hundreds of millions of pounds a year.

00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:14.323
Ben Sims of Turnstone Intelligence said he was surprised by the size of the gap in outcomes,

00:05:14.743 --> 00:05:17.843
and that the results support long-held suspicions in the industry.

00:05:18.864 --> 00:05:23.424
Audi confirmed it will build a $4 billion factory in the United States after Donald Trump

00:05:23.424 --> 00:05:25.424
announced the project at a Georgia rally.

00:05:25.944 --> 00:05:29.844
The German carmaker confirmed the plans after that election rally statement.

00:05:30.284 --> 00:05:33.144
Car production is expected to begin early next decade.

00:05:33.784 --> 00:05:38.664
Deutsche Wella noted the project's scale and the long gap before manufacturing starts, with

00:05:38.664 --> 00:05:43.164
This production not expected until the early 2030s, even after the immediate confirmation

00:05:43.164 --> 00:05:44.104
of the investment.

00:05:45.151 --> 00:05:49.831
Sydney's new international airport welcomed its first passengers, progress worth knowing

00:05:49.831 --> 00:05:53.391
after years of planning and construction in Australia's busiest city.

00:05:54.071 --> 00:05:58.971
Reuters reported the operational start of a major transport project that expands options for

00:05:58.971 --> 00:06:01.431
international travel in the country's largest city.

00:06:02.071 --> 00:06:05.071
The facility is designed to handle growing passenger volumes.

00:06:05.071 --> 00:06:11.163
The Falkland Islands government, Mercopress reported, urged residents who have not completed

00:06:11.163 --> 00:06:14.083
the 2026 census to submit returns promptly.

00:06:14.723 --> 00:06:19.183
United Kingdom Prime Minister Andy Burnham spoke with Chile's president Jose Antonio

00:06:19.183 --> 00:06:22.023
Cast about defense issues including the Falklands.

00:06:22.663 --> 00:06:27.963
Voters in Bulgaria chose a president in a contest viewed as a test of Prime Minister Roman Radevs

00:06:27.963 --> 00:06:32.263
popularity, with security concerns over Black Sea incidents in the background.

00:06:32.263 --> 00:06:38.111
To really understand how a closed frontier moves the price of cooking fuel and bread, skip

00:06:38.111 --> 00:06:40.311
the diplomatic readout and follow the trucks.

00:06:40.751 --> 00:06:44.971
A common misunderstanding treats a border shut down as little more than a signal between

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:45.571
governments.

00:06:46.091 --> 00:06:48.731
The working parts are simpler and closer to the kitchen.

00:06:49.331 --> 00:06:52.251
When a crossing shuts, cargo that use that road stops.

00:06:52.951 --> 00:06:58.291
In places with only a few gates, trade is already concentrated, so one closed route does

00:06:58.291 --> 00:06:59.451
not spread out evenly.

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:05.911
Shippers then reroute, rerouting adds time, fuel, and fees, and importers pass those costs

00:07:05.911 --> 00:07:11.551
onto consumers. Shortages can show up inside a few days, which is why household energy and

00:07:11.551 --> 00:07:17.071
grocery bills can jump well before any joint statement is issued. Periodic India Pakistan

00:07:17.071 --> 00:07:22.551
closures show the same pattern. Even a brief halt can leave price spikes that linger after the

00:07:22.551 --> 00:07:28.671
gates reopen, because restocking takes weeks, not hours. The last several times that cycle ran,

00:07:28.671 --> 00:07:34.211
prices did not fall the morning the trucks rolled again. Knowing that, a reopening story is more

00:07:34.211 --> 00:07:39.471
useful if it says which goods actually moved before the halt, and whether those loads have started

00:07:39.471 --> 00:07:44.701
crossing again. Cross-check official statements from the government's involved, with independent

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:50.521
reporting from outlets in each affected country. Customs figures and transport schedules often make

00:07:50.521 --> 00:07:56.198
concrete what diplomatic language leaves vague. One thing to verify later is whether official

00:07:56.198 --> 00:08:00.918
trade statistics show a rebound in the specific commodities that sat still during the halt.

